The thermal efficiency is calculated as the ratio of heat absorbed by water to the energy from coal. Given efficiency is 10%, we solve for water mass $ X $:  
$$
0.10 = \frac{X \cdot 4.2 \times 10^3 \cdot 50}{1.4 \cdot 3 \times 10^7}
$$  
Simplifying:  
$$
X = \frac{0.10 \cdot 1.4 \cdot 3 \times 10^7}{4.2 \times 10^3 \cdot 50} = \frac{4.2 \times 10^6}{2.1 \times 10^5} = 20 \text{ kg}
$$  
Final answer: \boxed{20 kg}

