$$
\Delta T = \frac{Q}{mc} = \frac{2.1 \times 10^7}{200 \times 4.2 \times 10^3} = 25^\circ\text{C}
$$  
The initial temperature was $ 22^\circ\text{C} $, so the final temperature $ [X] $ is:  
$$
X = 22 + 25 = 47^\circ\text{C}
$$  
