The pressure exerted by the car is calculated as $ P = \frac{(m_{\text{car}} + m_{\text{driver}})g}{A} $. Given $ P = 10^5 \, \text{Pa} $, $ g = 10 \, \text{N/kg} $, $ A = 0.1 \, \text{m}^2 $, and $ m_{\text{car}} = 950 \, \text{kg} $, solving for $ m_{\text{driver}} $:

$$
